{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Blessed of HaShem be his land, with the bounty of heaven.</b> He called the rains 'the bounty of heaven,' and this is the statement of the Sages, blessed be their memory: 'The upper waters are suspended by the utterance, and their fruit is rainwater.' And thus Scripture says (Psalms 104:13): ״משקה הרים מעליותיו מפרי מעשיך תשבע הארץ״ — 'He waters the mountains from His upper chambers; from the fruit of Your works the earth is sated' — for the heavens are His works, and likewise it is written (Psalms 8:4): ״כי אראה שמיך מעשה אצבעותיך״ — 'When I behold Your heavens, the work of Your fingers.' And He called the rains 'the fruit of His works,' that is to say, the fruit of the heavens, and this is ממגד שמים — 'the bounty of heaven.' And when He says ממגד שמים מטל — 'the bounty of heaven, for dew' — He blessed it with dew and with rain." "<b>And from the depth that couches beneath.</b> These are the lower waters, for with the upper waters and the lower waters He blessed it, and they are the light and the darkness. Therefore He joined the dew to the deep. And it is known that dew does not descend by day but at night. And thus Jacob mentioned in his blessing (Genesis 49:25): ״ברכות שמים מעל ברכות תהום רובצת תחת״ — 'blessings of heaven above, blessings of the deep that couches beneath.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:54:07.740561917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}